>
>  What do you consider useful stuff that the Board could do, and how does 
> it compare to the (in my opinion) very valuable work of teachers, 
> translators, artists, learners, and people involved in defining the 
> language (e.g. BPFK)?
>

The reason that LLG exists is to serve the teachers, translators, artists, 
learners, etc. In the words of the bylaws: 

The Logical Language Group, Inc. shall place priority on support of the 
community of persons learning, using, experimenting with, and promoting the 
language known as "Lojban - A Realization of Loglan" or alternatively 
"Lojban".


The board exists to represent the members of the organization whenever they 
are not meeting as a formal body, and so it has the same purpose, but 
higher expectations of participation.

An excellent reason for people to get involved with LLG, either at a 
membership or director level, is because they have ideas about how LLG can 
better support the lojban-using community.

